# Q Mobile: Core Accounting Model

All ledger and in/out entry logic must follow the **double-entry accounting model**. Full spec: `docs/CORE_ACCOUNTING_MODEL.md`.

## Core accounts (every transaction hits ≥ 2)

- **Accounts Receivable (Customer)** — AR  
- **Accounts Payable (Supplier)** — AP  
- **Driver Payable**  
- **Vehicle Expense**  
- **Revenue** · **Cash/Bank** · **Commission Expense**

## Mapping: current `transactions` row → double entry

| UI / payload | Stored as | Double entry (logical) |
|--------------|-----------|-------------------------|
| Cash IN, party = client | amount_in > 0, contact_type client | Dr Cash/Bank · Cr AR (customer payment) |
| Cash OUT, party = supplier | amount_out > 0, contact_type supplier | Dr AP · Cr Cash/Bank (supplier payment) |
| Cash OUT, party = driver | amount_out > 0, contact_type driver, description e.g. Monthly salary | Dr Driver Payable · Cr Cash/Bank (driver payment) |
| Cash OUT, vehicle expense (Fuel/Maintenance/Toll etc.) | amount_out > 0, no contact, party_name/description = expense type | Dr Vehicle Expense · Cr Cash/Bank |

Trip creation (asset): AR + Revenue; Commission Expense + Driver Payable; vehicle revenue allocation.  
Trip creation (aggregation): AR + Revenue; Cost of Service + AP; no vehicle.

## Rules

- **Balance is always computed** from transaction history; no direct balance editing.
- Trip rate edit → auto-adjust receivable; supplier rate edit → auto-adjust payable; trip cancellation → reverse entries.
- Ledger edit after 7 days → require admin approval (when implemented).
- Use `features/finance/accounting/accountingModel.ts` for consistent debit/credit account interpretation of a row.

## UI

Do not change existing Finance tab layout. Customers, Suppliers, Garage, Drivers, Ledger and entity details already align with the model; new work should preserve current UI and only adjust data flow and entry logic.
